# Rendering model

Rocci treats HTML as the shared boundary between build time, server time, and
the browser. JavaScript can enhance a page, but it is not the default unit of
composition.

## Components are Roc functions

An authored component lowers to a function that returns `Html`:

```text
@component Status = |{ label }| <strong>{label}</strong>
                         │
                         ▼
status = |{ label }| Html.element("strong", [], [Html.text(label)])
```

Component calls become ordinary function calls. Props are Roc records. A paired
tag passes its body as an additional `Html` argument.

## Documents and fragments are distinct

GET handlers are expected to return complete HTML documents. Mutation handlers
return fragments that the generated server encodes as Datastar patch events.

| Handler | Typical result | Browser behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@on:get` | `<html>...</html>` | Load or navigate a document |
| `@on:post` / `put` / `patch` / `delete` | Element with a stable target | Patch matching DOM |
| Authored long-lived SSE | Stream of events | Update over time |

This distinction prevents every fragment from carrying a document shell, CSS,
or script setup.

## CSS is colocated and scoped

File and component `@css` blocks are raw CSS. Lowering adds stable
`data-rocci-css` stamps and wraps rules in CSS `@scope`. A component author
keeps writing familiar selectors while separate components avoid accidental
global collisions.

The current compiler also injects styles for direct preview. A production
asset pipeline can extract the same `StyleArtifact` values and include them once.

## Datastar transports intent and HTML

An attribute such as `data-on:click=@post("/actions/save")` declares a browser
event and backend request. The handler returns HTML, not a client-state diff.
Datastar patches the matching element.

This gives server-owned data one authoritative representation. It also means
stable element IDs and focused fragment boundaries matter.

## Rocdown is static until made explicit

Markdown text, headings, tables, links, and fences are static. `@roc`,
`@render`, document-root Rocci tags, and handlers introduce executable regions
that are visible in source. Raw inline HTML is disabled by default.

## Rocdown pre-renders the documentation shell

Rocdown resolves every publishable page before output. It renders article HTML,
passes normalized site and navigation data to the Rocdown theme, and writes
ordinary static documents. Navigation and reading remain functional without
client JavaScript.

See [Architecture](/concepts/architecture/) for crate ownership or build a
working patch flow in [Server actions](/guides/server-actions/).
